WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:05.612
The question of whether incitement to riot is an&nbsp;impeachable offense is pretty easy.

00:00:05.612 --> 00:00:08.648
 Clearly, yes.

00:00:08.648 --> 00:00:12.000
From the beginning of this not normal&nbsp;presidency,

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:16.367
we've had a lot of talk about both impeachment and the 25th Amendment. 

00:00:16.367 --> 00:00:21.112
In most&nbsp;ordinary circumstances, if you can use that&nbsp;phrase in this context, 

00:00:21.112 --> 00:00:27.441
the 25th Amendment is&nbsp;a really a poor tool for removing a president.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.441 --> 00:00:34.560
It was really designed for presidents that were&nbsp;nearly completely incapacitated, Woodrow Wilson,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:40.140
after the stroke, James Garfield, dying of&nbsp;blood poisoning after the assassination attempt.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:44.360
It wasn't supposed to get rid of bad Presidents.

00:00:44.360 --> 00:00:47.535
We will stop the steal.

00:00:47.535 --> 00:00:53.759
All along during the Trump presidency, when&nbsp;this solution has been proposed, 

00:00:53.759 --> 00:00:57.749
I thought it was pretty unrealistic for a couple of reasons.&nbsp;

00:00:57.749 --> 00:01:04.774
The framers of the 25th Amendment deliberately made it harder to do than impeachment. 

00:01:04.774 --> 00:01:10.736
Impeachment only requires a super majority in the Senate for&nbsp;conviction, a majority in the House.

00:01:10.736 --> 00:01:15.899
In order for&nbsp;the switch, under the 25th Amendment, to stick

00:01:15.899 --> 00:01:21.000
it has to be ratified by Congress, and that requires a super majority in both houses.

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:26.003
If you do have a super majority in both houses, then&nbsp;you could just impeach him.

00:01:26.003 --> 00:01:28.715
And that's really the remedy.

00:01:28.715 --> 00:01:32.080
I think we may be in a different situation here, though.

00:01:32.080 --> 00:01:35.891
One of the main advantages, perhaps the only advantage,

00:01:35.891 --> 00:01:41.409
that the 25th Amendment offers over impeachment is speed. 

00:01:41.409 --> 00:01:46.553
If Mike Pence was&nbsp;willing to do this, and he had a majority of the cabinet behind him,

00:01:46.553 --> 00:01:48.541
you could do it in the next&nbsp;20 minutes. 

00:01:48.541 --> 00:01:51.173
And it takes effect immediately.

00:01:51.173 --> 00:01:56.593
In the past I’ve thought that one scenario where you might favor this

00:01:56.593 --> 00:02:03.000
is if the President were to give&nbsp;the order to launch an unprovoked nuclear strike.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:08.960
I certainly hope we are not in that sort of&nbsp;situation here, but you can understand 

00:02:08.960 --> 00:02:11.267
why people would worry about it.

00:02:11.267 --> 00:02:18.269
The argument for a&nbsp;25th Amendment solution here would be well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.269 --> 00:02:20.039
how lucky do you feel?

00:02:20.039 --> 00:02:27.601
Are we sure that what happened at the Capitol, after Trump's riot rally speech,  

00:02:27.601 --> 00:02:30.375
are we sure that that was peak Trump?

00:02:30.375 --> 00:02:35.432
In the remaining few days of his presidency, that's the worst we're going to see.

00:02:35.432 --> 00:02:37.448
Maybe it is.

00:02:37.448 --> 00:02:41.484
Do you want to think about how much you're willing to stake on that proposition?

00:02:41.484 --> 00:02:45.747
The argument for&nbsp;a last minute impeachment is a little different.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.747 --> 00:02:51.618
What impeachment does is it puts an additional&nbsp;black mark on a presidency, 

00:02:51.618 --> 00:02:54.289
an additional mark of disgrace and shame. 

00:02:54.289 --> 00:02:58.800
And it's a signal to the presidents that are going to follow  

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:05.200
that this black mark can be put on you even&nbsp;at the last moments of your presidency,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:09.271
if your behavior has been egregious enough. 

00:03:09.271 --> 00:03:14.705
Making Donald Trump the only president to have been  

00:03:14.705 --> 00:03:21.753
impeached twice would really underscore that&nbsp;point.

00:03:21.753 --> 00:03:26.395
I've long thought that America should impeach presidents more often,

00:03:26.395 --> 00:03:30.182
and perhaps this&nbsp;president more often.

00:03:30.182 --> 00:03:32.824
Impeachment is a broad remedy.

00:03:32.824 --> 00:03:37.758
High crimes and misdemeanors is a term of art that was designed to reach,

00:03:37.758 --> 00:03:46.560
and historically has reached, a wide variety of offenses that&nbsp;go to the person's fitness for high office.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.560 --> 00:03:52.490
Hamilton talked about impeachment in terms of the&nbsp;misconduct of public men,

00:03:52.490 --> 00:03:58.709
and said that it could notnot be limited in the way that criminal offenses&nbsp;were limited.

00:03:58.709 --> 00:04:04.189
Madison said the impeachment was the indispensable remedy for incapacity, negligence, 

00:04:04.189 --> 00:04:06.859
or perfidy in the chief magistrate.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.859 --> 00:04:14.266
It was not viewed, as it too often is today,&nbsp;as itself an agent of constitutional crisis.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.266 --> 00:04:19.266
Impeachment was viewed as the solution to a constitutional crisis.

00:04:19.266 --> 00:04:26.000
If anything, I think they would be surprised&nbsp;that we've resorted to it so infrequently.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:33.760
One thing that has always troubled me is&nbsp;this argument that well, impeachment,

00:04:33.760 --> 00:04:35.198
it's like a coup.

00:04:35.198 --> 00:04:39.490
It's terribly anti-democratic. It's disruptive. 

00:04:39.490 --> 00:04:46.690
When you look at the events of the last week or so, I don't ever want to hear again,

00:04:46.690 --> 00:04:50.439
that it's impeachment that's a constitutional&nbsp;crisis.

00:04:50.439 --> 00:04:55.153
That it's impeachment, that's disruptive,&nbsp;and anti-democratic. &nbsp;

00:04:55.153 --> 00:04:58.118
I think that argument deserves to be laughed out of court, 

00:04:58.118 --> 00:05:02.457
given what we've experienced over the last few days.

